         fhir:equivalence [ fhir:v "wider" ] ;
         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element `Task.requestedPeriod` has a context of Task based on following the parent source element upwards and mapping to `Task`.\nElement `Task.requestedPeriod` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nThis is typically used when the Task is *not* seeking fulfillment of a focus Request, as in that case the period would be specified on the Request and/or in the Task.restriction.period.  Instead, it is used for stand-alone tasks." ]
